The new foldable <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> is the "thinnest iPhone ever," according to Apple. When unfolded, the device is 5.2mm thick, making it 0.4mm thinner than the 5.6mm <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-air/">iPhone Air</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-side.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="899" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063436" /><br/>
Rumors suggested it could be <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/02/25/iphone-fold-crease-measured-production/">as thin as 4.5mm</a> when unfolded, similar to Samsung's Galaxy Z Fold8, but it didn't end up that thin. At 5.2mm, it's just a little bit thicker than the 5.1mm 13-inch <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-pro/">iPad Pro</a>, which is Apple's thinnest device.<br/>
<br/>
When folded, the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; is 11.3mm thick. For comparison, the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17-pro/">iPhone 17 Pro</a> Max and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> Max are both 8.75mm thick.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; is also Apple's heaviest iPhone to date at 254 grams, which is five grams heavier than the 249-gram &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max. It has a 7.6-inch inner display when it's open and a 5.4-inch outer display when it's closed, and it has a short, wide design.<br/>
